characteristic_form:
The agent confirms the data window with iot.stream_extent for Transformer 1 at MAIN. It retrieves per-sample gas and oil-quality values with iot.history.

It identifies the first and last samples in which hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene, acetylene, co, co2, oxygen, nitrogen, dbds, interfacial_v and dielectric_rigidity are all non-null. If a boundary sample is incomplete, it moves to the next complete sample inward and reports the timestamps it used.

It calls fmsr.predict_health_index for each selected sample and reports the timestamp, score and condition category of each. It then computes the score delta and applies the 5-point noise threshold, labelling a change below 5 points as 'stable'.

If the score declined by 5 points or more, the agent:
- ranks the two or three inputs with the largest percentage change;
- attributes the decline mainly to fault gases or mainly to oil quality;
- maps the drivers to one failure mode obtained via fmsr.get_failure_modes;
- corroborates that mode with fmsr.interpret_dga on the last sample (hydrogen, methane, acetylene, ethylene, ethane) and gives a high, medium or low confidence.

In all cases it recommends one concrete next check, such as a confirmatory resample, an oil quality retest or an OLTC compartment sample.

Fallback: if only one complete sample exists, the agent reports that single health index, states that no trend can be judged, and bases the failure-mode call on the fmsr.interpret_dga result for that sample. The agent must not impute missing inputs.
